---
/**
 * Track 4 (Visual Math: Linear Algebra), Lesson 12, illustration 1 of 2.
 *
 * The Cramer-rule setup. The parallelogram spanned by the unknown vector
 * [x, y] and j-hat has signed area equal to x. j-hat is the base of length
 * 1 along the y-axis; the height (the perpendicular distance from j-hat's
 * line to [x, y]) is x. Picture-proof: det([[x, 0], [y, 1]]) = x. With
 * a concrete (x, y) = (2, 1), the area is 2.
 */

const cx = 220;
const cy = 270;
const u = 55;

const X_MIN = -1;
const X_MAX = 4;
const Y_MIN = -1;
const Y_MAX = 3;

const sx = (gx: number) => cx + gx * u;
const sy = (gy: number) => cy - gy * u;

const xs: number[] = [];
for (let i = X_MIN; i < X_MAX + 1; i++) xs.push(i);
const ys: number[] = [];
for (let j = Y_MIN; j < Y_MAX + 1; j++) ys.push(j);

const xVal = 2;
const yVal = 1;
const j = { x: 0, y: 1 };
const unk = { x: xVal, y: yVal };

const TEAL = '#0d9488';
const AMBER = '#d97706';
const ACCENT = '#7c3aed';
---

<figure class="cw-illus">
	<svg viewBox="0 0 740 360" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-labelledby="la-cramer1-title la-cramer1-desc">
		<title id="la-cramer1-title">The parallelogram spanned by [x, y] and j-hat has signed area equal to x</title>
		<desc id="la-cramer1-desc">A two-dimensional coordinate grid. An amber arrow shows j-hat from the origin to [0, 1], the base of length 1 along the y axis. A purple arrow shows the unknown vector [x, y] equal to [2, 1] from the origin. The two together span a parallelogram with corners at the origin, [2, 1], [2, 2], and [0, 1], filled in light accent purple. A dashed horizontal segment marks the height of x equals 2 from the y axis to the right edge of the parallelogram. The label "signed area = x = 2" sits in the center of the parallelogram.</desc>

		<defs>
			<marker id="la-cramer1-arrow-j" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto">
				<path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill={AMBER} />
			</marker>
			<marker id="la-cramer1-arrow-x" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="9" markerHeight="9" orient="auto">
				<path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill={ACCENT} />
			</marker>
		</defs>

		{xs.map((i) => <line x1={sx(i)} y1={sy(Y_MIN)} x2={sx(i)} y2={sy(Y_MAX)} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5" opacity="0.10" />)}
		{ys.map((jj) => <line x1={sx(X_MIN)} y1={sy(jj)} x2={sx(X_MAX)} y2={sy(jj)} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5" opacity="0.10" />)}
		<line x1={sx(X_MIN)} y1={sy(0)} x2={sx(X_MAX)} y2={sy(0)} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.45" />
		<line x1={sx(0)} y1={sy(Y_MIN)} x2={sx(0)} y2={sy(Y_MAX)} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.45" />

		{/* parallelogram */}
		<path d={`M ${sx(0)} ${sy(0)} L ${sx(unk.x)} ${sy(unk.y)} L ${sx(unk.x)} ${sy(unk.y + 1)} L ${sx(j.x)} ${sy(j.y)} Z`} fill={ACCENT} fill-opacity="0.18" stroke={ACCENT} stroke-width="1.4" />

		{/* height marker: dashed horizontal at the midpoint of j-hat side */}
		<line x1={sx(0)} y1={sy(0.5)} x2={sx(unk.x)} y2={sy(0.5)} stroke={ACCENT} stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="4 4" opacity="0.6" />
		<text x={sx(unk.x / 2)} y={sy(0.5) - 6} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>height = x = {xVal}</text>

		{/* arrows */}
		<line x1={sx(0)} y1={sy(0)} x2={sx(j.x)} y2={sy(j.y)} stroke={AMBER} stroke-width="3" marker-end="url(#la-cramer1-arrow-j)" />
		<line x1={sx(0)} y1={sy(0)} x2={sx(unk.x)} y2={sy(unk.y)} stroke={ACCENT} stroke-width="2.8" marker-end="url(#la-cramer1-arrow-x)" />

		<circle cx={sx(0)} cy={sy(0)} r="3" fill="currentColor" />

		<text x={sx(j.x) - 8} y={sy(j.y) + 4} text-anchor="end" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill={AMBER}>ĵ</text>
		<text x={sx(unk.x) + 8} y={sy(unk.y) - 6} font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>[x, y] = [{xVal}, {yVal}]</text>

		<text x={sx(unk.x / 2 + 0.1)} y={sy(1.4) + 4} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>signed area = x = {xVal}</text>

		{/* legend */}
		<g transform="translate(450, 100)">
			<rect x="0" y="0" width="260" height="120" rx="6" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.04" />
			<rect x="0" y="0" width="260" height="120" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8" opacity="0.3" />
			<text x="130" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">why area = x:</text>
			<text x="130" y="48" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="12" fill="currentColor">
				base · height = 1 · x = x
			</text>
			<text x="130" y="72" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.8">
				det([[x, 0], [y, 1]]) = x
			</text>
			<text x="130" y="100" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill={TEAL}>
				the unknown x IS this area
			</text>
		</g>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>j-hat is a base of length 1 along y; the unknown [x, y] reaches out to the right. The parallelogram they span has signed area exactly equal to x, because its base is 1 and its height (the rightward reach) is x. The unknown coordinate is geometrically just an area.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.cw-illus { margin: 1.75rem auto; max-width: 100%; }
	.cw-illus svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 740px; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; }
	.cw-illus figcaption { text-align: center; font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.75; margin-top: 0.5rem; font-style: italic; }
</style>
